Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:07.829 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  so i just played through the age of  calamity demo  twice actually and i don't really want  to do any more theorizing on the story  or the plot  of the game since we're already so close  to release now and nintendo is just  putting out so much stuff at this point  that i feel more comfortable just  waiting until the game comes out so  rest assured there's not going to be any  spoilers in terms of the plot of the  game  instead let's break down link's moveset  and some of the crazy combos you can do  now for some of you who are familiar  with the warriors games this might all  be  nothing new but for those who are not  and have only played breath of the wild  this might be more interesting you will  be pleased to know that the characters  have an idol animation  so that's nice anyway down to business  movement left control stick to move  around right control stick to control  the camera  same as in breath of the wild you can  walk by tilting the control stick in any  direction and go into a jog by tilting  it all the way  if you hold it all the way long enough  link will eventually start running  you can perform a dodge by pressing b if  the control stick is in the neutral  position you will do a back flip  or you can use the control stick to  dodge in any direction even diagonally  you can do it pretty quickly too which  looks kind of funny to be honest  something that's good to know is that it  takes quite a while for link to  transition from a jog  into a run but if you perform a forward  dodge while moving forward he will start  running much quicker  do take note that you need to hold b  briefly and not tap it too quickly or  else it doesn't work  you can also go straight into a run from  a standstill without the dodge animation  by pressing b  and forward at the same time but unlike  in breath of the wild you don't need to  hold down b  to keep running after link goes into a  sprint you can just let go of b  next is strafing pressing and holding  down zl will allow you to move around at  walking speed while facing the same  direction  this also makes link hold up his shield  so it doubles as a guard  unlike in breath of the wild however  this doesn't function as a lock-on  mechanic  locking onto enemies is still a thing  but it's done by pressing the right  control stick and you don't need to hold  it  just one click and you're locked on and  you can switch targets by pressing the  right control stick again while strafing  you can still  dodge forward back left and right  however you can dodge diagonally like  before  if you press and hold b after a dodge  and tilt the control stick in any  direction it will cancel guard mode  and makes you sprint in any direction  upon landing now on to the good stuff  attacking and combos so there's three  basic attacks  regular strong and a unique action  regular attacks are performed with y  continuously tapping the button will  perform a basic string you start off  with four swings but in my case i  already unlocked the fifth one and it's  safe to assume that these will be  expanded even further in the full game  in breath of the wild once you start  swinging you can change direction  however in age of calamity you can  next is the strong attacks which you  perform by pressing x  you can also press and hold down x to  charge it up and you can even move while  it's charged now a strong attack on its  own  isn't really that interesting or  effective but combining it with regular  attacks is where the real fun begins  you can cancel your regular attack combo  into a strong move  you can do this by simply performing a  regular string with y and then switch to  x at any point  the strong move will be different  depending on the amount of regular  attacks you performed before it so after  one swing  two swings three swings or four  you can switch to a strong attack at any  point in the combo  except after the finisher now here's  where it gets even more fun  most of the strong moves performed mid  combo can be charged as well by holding  the button down  so for example if you perform a regular  attack then a strong one but instead of  just tapping it you hold the button down  once released the move will be expanded  even further  this doesn't work for every strong  attack but it does for all moves that  follow up from your regular string of  attacks  then we have the unique action performed  with zr which in link's case is using  his bow to fire off a flurry of arrows  link's got quite the drawing hand there  you can aim before or during the attack  by tilting the left control stick  interestingly enough this action has  priority over regular attacks and strong  attacks  so even while you're in the middle of  one of your other attacks pressing zr  will cancel it out  in turn the unique action can also be  cancelled out before the attack by  pressing b  or can be interrupted early by dodging  and then we have the special attack  which can only be performed when this  meter is full simply press a when the  meter is full and you're good to go  but we're not done yet there's a couple  of more things to cover  firstly you can perform either a regular  or a strong attack from a run  a dash attack where link thrusts his  sword forwards or a long shield serve  there's also a shorter shield serve but  that one is part of the regular attack  combo after the second swing  both attacks can be expanded with a  regular combo however you can't follow  up with a strong attack while shield  surfing  neither can you charge it like with the  shorter variant  pressing the regular attack button while  shielding will trigger a shield bash  this can be used to parry or reflect  guardian lasers  also note that after the shield bash you  can continue to hit y to perform your  regular sword swings  next we have aerial attacks and  paragliding there's a couple of  different ways to get airborne in this  game  using cryonis certain strong attacks or  by wall jumping  you can wall jump by dodging into a wall  by pressing b  and then immediately press b again  basically a quick double tap  simply running or walking into a wall  won't work you can even backflip into a  wall and it will still do the job  aside from walls you can also use trees  or any other object that is high enough  even the cryoness pillars you created  yourself once you're airborne you can do  a number of different things  activate the paraglider with b perform a  string of regular attacks  a strong attack or activate your bow  some can even be performed in succession  like the paraglider first  then into a regular attack and then  finish off with a strong attack or your  bow  you don't have to use the paraglider by  the way you can also just skip right to  attack  do keep in mind that you cannot  paraglide after an attack  nor can you do any follow-ups after a  strong attack or your unique action  with all this stuff combined you can  perform some pretty long and nifty  combos so  experiment away and of course as stated  before most of these attacks will likely  be expanded further in the later parts  of the game and there might be many more  possibilities with other weapons like  spears or two-handed weapons  but i think this is already a pretty  strong basis  lastly i will briefly touch upon some of  the other controls  pressing and holding down r will bring  up the four different runes which you  then choose with y  x a or b you got stasis to freeze  enemies in front of you  bombs to uh well bomb stuff the  aforementioned cryoness to launch  yourself upwards and magnesius to grab  iron objects to use against your enemies  the effects of the runes differ from  character to character and also from  situation to situation  for example cryonis can also be used to  counter charging enemies  so i'm not going to go further into them  as of right now  pressing and holding l brings up the  item menu these include any special  weapons you picked up like fire rods or  ice rods and food to replenish your  health  and as is with the runes there's also  more situational attacks  such as a weakness finisher which can be  performed after breaking a strong  enemy's defense and probably much more  but those kinda speak for themselves and  usually it comes down to  pressing the right button at the right  time so that pretty much covers it for  now  i hope that this was of some use to you  and if not  at least entertaining enough to watch of  course everything covered here only  applies to the beginning of the game and  will likely get a lot more crazy down  the line  anyway i will see you next time

